-- חוזר לבעלויות תש"פ/7 (2.4.2020): הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד מיום 1.4.2020 – עובדי
-- הוראה בתקופת חירום (נגיף הקורונה).
-- Teaching during the coronavirus emergency (15.3.2020–18.4.2020): studies
-- go on through the spring holidays, salary is unchanged, and teachers on
-- unpaid leave or substitutes work the extended school year in proportion.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT daydate

§ `תש"פ/7 הסכם קיבוצי מיוחד 1.4.2020 – עובדי הוראה בתקופת חירום`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, circular number, address, date, reference number, addressees, greeting and subject line; no rule.

§§ `Background and the application period`

@desc An employee and employer as far as the leave regulations ask.
DECLARE `employment under the leave regulations` HAS
    `bound by another collective agreement`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `that agreement signed before or during the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that agreement approved by the wages commissioner`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `that agreement takes no statutory right beyond the leave agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

@desc A teaching employee as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `emergency employee` HAS
    `graded on the teaching-employee scale`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed in the state service`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an owning body`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `stage`                                        IS AN `emergency stage`
    `days set by the Director-General's circular`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc study and holiday days set by the Director-General's circulars of 2.4.2019

DECLARE `emergency stage` IS ONE OF
    `kindergarten`
    `primary`
    `junior high`
    `special education`
    `upper secondary`

DECLARE `emergency action` IS ONE OF
    `hold studies on the day`
    `work the extended days` HAS `days worked` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the salary` HAS `amount paid` IS A NUMBER

-- ¶19: the Public Health Order bars any activity gathering teachers or
-- pupils until 18.4.2020.
@ref akn:preamble/p19
`the last day the Public Health Order bars gatherings` MEANS Date 18 4 2020

-- ¶20: under the emergency regulations extending the leave agreement to the
-- wider public sector, the "leave agreement" does not apply to an employee
-- and public employer bound by another collective agreement, signed before
-- or while the regulations are in force and approved by the wages
-- commissioner, provided it takes from the employee no statutory right
-- beyond what the leave agreement would.
@ref akn:preamble/p20
GIVEN x IS AN `employment under the leave regulations`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the leave agreement applies` x IF
    NOT (    x's `bound by another collective agreement`
         AND x's `that agreement signed before or during the regulations`
         AND x's `that agreement approved by the wages commissioner`
         AND x's `that agreement takes no statutory right beyond the leave agreement`)

-- ¶21–22: the agreement of 1.4.2020 covers teaching employees graded on the
-- teaching scale, employed IN THE STATE SERVICE, whose study and holiday
-- days are set by the Director-General's circulars of 2.4.2019 (notices 143,
-- 144, 145), and it is an "other agreement" under the regulations for them.
@ref akn:preamble/p21
GIVEN e IS AN `emergency employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 1.4.2020 covers` e IF
        e's `graded on the teaching-employee scale`
    AND e's `employed in the state service`
    AND e's `days set by the Director-General's circular`

@ref akn:preamble/p22
GIVEN e IS AN `emergency employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is an other agreement for` e IF
    `the agreement of 1.4.2020 covers` e

-- ¶23: the circular governs studies and employment during the emergency,
-- and the leave regulations, from 15.3.2020 to 18.4.2020 inclusive
-- ("תקופת התחולה").
@ref akn:preamble/p23
`the application period begins` MEANS Date 15 3 2020
@ref akn:preamble/p23
`the application period ends` MEANS Date 18 4 2020

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days in the application period` IS
    Day `the application period ends` MINUS Day `the application period begins` PLUS 1

§§ `א. Who the circular covers`

-- F-2019-20_tashaf_07-b: §א reaches every teaching employee "בבעלויות" in
-- the stages it lists, while the agreement it implements (¶21) covers only
-- teachers in the state service.
@ref akn:art_a/p1
GIVEN e IS AN `emergency employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular covers` e IF
        e's `graded on the teaching-employee scale`
    AND e's `employed by an owning body`
    AND (   e's `stage` EQUALS `kindergarten`
         OR e's `stage` EQUALS `primary`
         OR e's `stage` EQUALS `junior high`
         OR (e's `stage` EQUALS `special education` AND e's `days set by the Director-General's circular`))

§§ `ב. Studies through the holidays`

DECLARE `sector` IS ONE OF
    `Jewish sector`
    `Arab sector`
    `mixed institution`
    `Druze institution teaching on Saturday`
    `Druze institution not teaching on Saturday`

-- §ב's list of holiday days on which studies are held all the same.
@ref akn:art_b/p1 akn:art_b__para_a/p1 akn:art_b__para_b/p1 akn:art_b__para_c/p1 akn:art_b__para_d/p1
GIVEN s IS A `sector`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a holiday day on which studies are held` s d IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `Jewish sector` THEN d AT LEAST Date 31 3 2020 AND d AT MOST Date 3 4 2020
    WHEN `Arab sector`   THEN d AT LEAST Date 6 4 2020  AND d AT MOST Date 9 4 2020
    WHEN `mixed institution` THEN
           d EQUALS Date 6 4 2020
        OR d EQUALS Date 8 4 2020
        OR d EQUALS Date 15 4 2020
    WHEN `Druze institution teaching on Saturday`     THEN d AT LEAST Date 28 3 2020 AND d AT MOST Date 31 3 2020
    WHEN `Druze institution not teaching on Saturday` THEN d AT LEAST Date 29 3 2020 AND d AT MOST Date 1 4 2020

-- §ב(ג): a mixed institution's fourth day is set by the institution with the
-- general supervision and the district, no later than 16.4.2020.
@ref akn:art_b__para_c/p1
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid fourth day for a mixed institution` d IF
    d AT MOST Date 16 4 2020

-- §ב ¶2: and on the ordinary study days of the application period.
@ref akn:art_b/p2
GIVEN s IS A `sector`, d IS A DATE, `an ordinary study day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `studies are held on` s d `an ordinary study day` IF
        d AT LEAST `the application period begins`
    AND d AT MOST `the application period ends`
    AND (`an ordinary study day` OR `a holiday day on which studies are held` s d)

-- One study day, as a duty: days from the day's start.
@ref akn:art_b/p1
GIVEN s IS A `sector`, d IS A DATE, `an ordinary study day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `emergency action`
DECIDE `holding studies` s d `an ordinary study day` IS
    IF `studies are held on` s d `an ordinary study day`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `hold studies on the day`
         WITHIN 1
         LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "תש\"פ/7 §ב: studies are held by the curriculum, holidays of §ב included"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `ג.–ד. The school year and salary`

-- akn:art_c/p1 An announcement that the new end of the school year will be notified later; it sets no date and binds no one yet.

-- §ד: "subject to chapters ב and ג", salary is unchanged until the end of the
-- application period; report-dependent components keep their own rules.
-- F-2019-20_tashaf_07-a: chapter ג imposes nothing on a teacher — it only
-- announces a later notice — so the condition it adds cannot be tested.
-- Reading adopted: the condition is chapter ב alone (with ג read as the
-- teacher's duty to work the extended year once it is announced, which §ה
-- spells out).
@ref akn:art_d/p1
GIVEN `held studies as chapter ב requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regular salary`                 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary through the application period` `held studies as chapter ב requires` `the regular salary` IS
    IF `held studies as chapter ב requires`
    THEN JUST `the regular salary`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ה. Unpaid leave and substitutes`

-- §ה ¶1–2: a teacher on unpaid leave (maternity leave included) for the whole
-- application period does not work the extension; one on leave for part of
-- it works the extension in proportion to the part not on leave.
@ref akn:art_e/p1 akn:art_e/p2
GIVEN `days of unpaid leave in the application period` IS A NUMBER
      `days the school year is extended`               IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `extension days a teacher works` `days of unpaid leave in the application period` `days the school year is extended` IS
    `days the school year is extended`
    TIMES (`days in the application period` MINUS `days of unpaid leave in the application period`)
    DIVIDED BY `days in the application period`

-- §ה ¶3 and (א): a substitute for a fixed period inside the application
-- period makes up days: the extension days, in proportion to the
-- substitution period out of the application period.
@ref akn:art_e/p3 akn:art_e__para_a/p1
GIVEN `days of substitution in the application period` IS A NUMBER
      `days the school year is extended`               IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days a substitute makes up` `days of substitution in the application period` `days the school year is extended` IS
    `days the school year is extended`
    TIMES `days of substitution in the application period`
    DIVIDED BY `days in the application period`

-- §ה(ב)–(ג): only once studies resume as they were before the Order, and from
-- the end of the substitute's assigned period to the end of the school year.
@ref akn:art_e__para_b/p1 akn:art_e__para_c/p1
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `studies resumed on`          IS A DATE
      `the assigned period ends on` IS A DATE
      `the school year ends on`     IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a substitute may make up a day on` d `studies resumed on` `the assigned period ends on` `the school year ends on` IF
        d AT LEAST `studies resumed on`
    AND d GREATER THAN `the assigned period ends on`
    AND d AT MOST `the school year ends on`

-- Time in days from the start of the make-up window.
GIVEN `days owed` IS A NUMBER, `days in the window` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `emergency action`
DECIDE `making up the days` `days owed` `days in the window` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `work the extended days` `days worked`
          PROVIDED `days worked` AT LEAST `days owed`
    WITHIN `days in the window`
    LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "תש\"פ/7 §ה: the days are made up by the end of the school year"

-- akn:art_e/p4 Wishes for health; no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, signatures and copies list; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples.
`an owners' kindergarten teacher` MEANS
    `emergency employee` WITH
        `graded on the teaching-employee scale`       IS TRUE
        `employed in the state service`               IS FALSE
        `employed by an owning body`                  IS TRUE
        `stage`                                       IS `kindergarten`
        `days set by the Director-General's circular` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `days in the application period` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `a holiday day on which studies are held` `Jewish sector` (Date 2 4 2020)
#ASSERT NOT `a holiday day on which studies are held` `Jewish sector` (Date 6 4 2020)
#ASSERT `a holiday day on which studies are held` `Druze institution teaching on Saturday` (Date 28 3 2020)
#ASSERT NOT `a holiday day on which studies are held` `Druze institution not teaching on Saturday` (Date 28 3 2020)
#ASSERT NOT `studies are held on` `Arab sector` (Date 20 4 2020) TRUE
#ASSERT `extension days a teacher works` 35 10 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `extension days a teacher works` 0 10 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `days a substitute makes up` 14 10 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the salary through the application period` TRUE 9000 EQUALS JUST 9000

-- A teacher on leave for 21 of the 35 days, with a 10-day extension, owes 4
-- days; working 4 within the window meets the duty, working 2 leaves it owed.
#TRACE `making up the days` (`extension days a teacher works` 21 10) 20 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `work the extended days` 4 AT 15
#TRACE `making up the days` (`extension days a teacher works` 21 10) 20 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `work the extended days` 2 AT 15
#TRACE `holding studies` `Jewish sector` (Date 1 4 2020) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `hold studies on the day` AT 0

-- The findings' evidence.
-- What chapter ג requires of a teaching employee, as printed: nothing.
GIVETH A LIST OF `emergency action`
DECIDE `what chapter ג requires of a teacher` IS EMPTY

`§ד conditions salary on a chapter that requires nothing of the teacher` MEANS
    `what chapter ג requires of a teacher` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `§ד conditions salary on a chapter that requires nothing of the teacher`

`a teacher of an owning body outside the state service is covered by the circular and not by the agreement it implements` MEANS
        `the circular covers` `an owners' kindergarten teacher`
    AND (NOT `the agreement of 1.4.2020 covers` `an owners' kindergarten teacher`)
#ASSERT `a teacher of an owning body outside the state service is covered by the circular and not by the agreement it implements`
